From 6758dd63a0a98720303d8110acc88035e10c37f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for Kush)" <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:31:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] remix api: textures from memory and file, config layers

CreateTextureFromMemory converts pixels on the caller thread (BGRA
swizzle, DX/OGL tangent normals to unsigned octahedral), then creates a
device-local image on the CS thread, uploads mip 0 and generates the
chain with the existing GenerateMipmap pass (max filter for height
maps). UpdateTextureFromMemory validates the whole batch first, applies
the patches and regenerates mips once per entry. CreateTextureFromFile
uses the asset loader the 0.6.6 runtime used for material paths.
DestroyTexture drops the API reference; materials keep theirs.

Config layers map onto RtxOptionManager layers: acquire waits for its
CS operation, a new layer starts disabled at strength 0, blending
requests resolve with option updates, and the last release removes the
layer. Shutdown releases API textures, retained instances and layers
while the device still exists.

Linux-only debug export remixlinux_GetApiResourceStats. Optional
REMIX_LINUX_COLOR_UNORM_AS_SRGB=1 samples 8-bit UNORM color textures as
sRGB, for comparison during GPU bring-up.

